C03: overheard speech gets its own clarification, no request found and does the person need something (DIALOGUE1513)

DIALOGUE1281 left the long stretches of other people's talk or broadcasts caught by the microphone to the model, which reconstructed the fragment, attributed itself the signature or answered as if addressed. `_unresolved_input_kind` now names «overheard_speech»: fifteen words or more, no question, no order verb at the start of a clause (a verb followed by a comma is a discourse marker), no vocative. `clarify_unresolved_input` composes a validated question for it: it says it finds no request for BAXY in what arrived and asks whether the person needs something; it rejects repeating five consecutive words of the talk, answering it or inventing an action, with one corrected retry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


